{{Politics of Balisca}}

'''Conservatism in Balisca''' ({{Langx|bl|conservatismo}}) emphasizes [[W:Minarchy|limited authority]] and [[W:Social equity|social equity]] stemming from [[W:Liberation theology|liberation theological]] theory, and generally alignes with [[W:One-nation conservatism|one-nation conservatism]] rather than [[W:Anti-statism|anti-statism]] and [[W:Social anarchism|social anarchism]]. Many Baliscan conservatives reject [[W:Individualism|individualism]] or [[W:Classical liberal|classical liberal]] principles and differ from modern Western conservatism because of the ideology's strong [[W:Communitarian|communitarian]] elements. A major concern of modern Baliscan conservatism is the preservation of so-called "[[Baliscan values]]", reflecting [[W:Cultural conservatism|cultural conservative]] tendencies. 

